docs {
  # Enduser connections: available users, instance users, resource rights and Altinn 2 roles

  BDD scenarios for four endpoints under `/accessmanagement/api/v1/enduser/connections`:

  - `GET users`: the parties the selected party already has a connection to, which the
    portal offers as recipients of a new delegation.
  - `GET resources/instances/users`: the parties that have access to one app instance.
  - `PUT resources/rights`: replaces the rights one party has delegated to another on a
    single resource.
  - `DELETE roles`: removes an Altinn 2 role assignment between two parties.

  Each subfolder is one scenario. The files inside are the scenario steps, named
  `NN_GIVEN|WHEN|THEN|AND|CLEANUP_...` and ordered by `seq`. A scenario starts from a known
  state (the GIVEN steps reset leftovers from earlier runs) and removes everything it
  created, so the folder can run repeatedly against a shared environment.

  ## Personas and fixtures

  Seed data comes from `testdata/enduser-connections-users-rights/<env>.js`, which only
  maps personas from `testdata/be-om-tilgang` and `testdata/enduser_instans-delegation`
  to the roles below:

  - delegator: a private person who owns an app instance and delegates access.
  - receiver: a private person the delegator makes rightholder and delegates to. The
    scenarios own the connection between the delegator and the receiver.
  - outsider: a private person with no relation to the delegator, used for the
    authorization negatives.

  Every step mints its own personal token through `helpers.js` (`loginAs(persona, scopes?)`).

  ## Environments

  Runs against AT22.
}
